PRIVILEGED & CONFIDENTIAL - prepared at the request of counsel. Please do not forward outside the addressee list.

Hi all,

You are receiving this because you are on the custodian list for a legal hold. Reference LH-2024-003. I know the word "hold" makes people nervous. Nobody is in trouble. It simply means that from now on you must keep everything that could be relevant, exactly as it is, until I tell you in writing that you can stop.

WHY

On 28 June Oakhaven Dairy's solicitors (Marlowe Pinfold LLP, Manchester) sent us a letter of claim over the temperature excursion on their load on 14 June, quantifying their loss at EUR 311,800. We have not admitted anything and we are talking to them, but a court dispute is reasonably foreseeable, so Polish law and good practice both require us to preserve the evidence now. Our outside counsel on this is Aurelia Hartwig at Hartwig Mielczarek i Wspólnicy in Gdańsk. She has seen the draft of this notice.

WHAT YOU MUST KEEP

Everything in any form (e-mail, Teams chats, WhatsApp, texts, paper, notebooks, photos, screenshots, drafts, voice notes, exports from Tidewalk and ColdLedger) that relates to Oakhaven Dairy Ltd or to the consignment of 14 June, for the period from 1 May 2024 until further notice. That includes in particular:

- the KC-Tag 4 readings and the KC-Hub 200 gateway logs for the container concerned;
- Tidewalk audit logs, alert history and the call log showing who was notified and when;
- dispatch notes, shift handover sheets and the group chat "Owls Dispatch" used by the night shift;
- GDY-1 gate and yard CCTV from 14:00 on 13 June to 14:00 on 15 June 2024;
- the maintenance record for the reefer unit and the pre-trip inspection sheet;
- anything you wrote or said afterwards about what happened, including the quick "what went wrong" notes.

WHAT YOU MUST NOT DO

Do not delete, edit, "tidy up", rename or move any of it. Do not write new commentary or opinions about the cause in chats or e-mail: if you need to say something about the incident, tell me by phone and I will tell you how to put it. Do not talk to anyone at Oakhaven or their solicitors about the dispute. Normal operational contact with their transport desk about live loads carries on as usual, but nothing about 14 June. Questions from anyone outside the company go to me.

IT ACTIONS - Kamil, please confirm each one to me by e-mail

1. Suspend the 90-day purge of raw Tidewalk telemetry for the Oakhaven account, and for the container, by 17:00 on 10 July 2024.
2. Suspend the 180-day auto-delete on the mailboxes of everyone on the list above.
3. Export the 30-day rolling CCTV footage for the window above before it is overwritten. The system overwrites after 30 days, so the footage for 13 June goes on 13 July; please do it tomorrow, not Friday.
4. Switch off disappearing messages on the WhatsApp group "Owls Dispatch" and set the Teams retention for the dispatch channel to "keep".
5. Take a forensic snapshot of the dispatch workstation at GDY-1 used on the 14 June night shift (Olek knows which desk). Do not log into it before the snapshot.

TIMING AND REVIEW

Please reply "ACKNOWLEDGED LH-2024-003" to this e-mail by 12:00 on 16 July 2024. I will chase non-responders on the 17th. The hold stays in place until I release it in writing, and I will review it every 90 days; the first review is due on 7 October 2024. A release does not happen by silence, by the claim going quiet, or because someone thinks it is finished.

If you think you hold relevant material that is not on this list, tell me, do not decide for yourself that it is irrelevant. If in doubt, keep it.

I am at ext. 4417 and on +48 58 555 0160. Out of hours, Benedikta has the incident desk on +48 58 555 0199.

Thank you, and sorry for the stress. Keep calm and don't delete.

Sofia

